  "_comment": "Tier config for scripts/seed-on-start.mjs. Edit this file, not the runner. All tiers (1-4) run by default; narrow with SEED_TIERS=1,2. Tier 4 is generated by scripts/wire-all-seeders.mjs (entries marked auto:true; rerun it after adding a seeder). 'script' is the file name in scripts/ without .mjs. 'freshMinutes' = skip on next start if the last OK run is younger than this. 'requiresAnyEnv' = run only if at least one of these env vars is non-empty (otherwise recorded as SKIP without spawning). 'timeoutSec' overrides the default per-seeder timeout. Tier-1 membership is based on static reading of each seeder's process.env usage and has NOT yet been confirmed by running every seeder; see the handoff report. Every scripts/seed-*.mjs is now either in a tier or in 'excluded' with a reason (bundles, non-seeders, upstream-host warm-pings). seed-insights.mjs (news:insights:v1, used by get_news_intelligence) is a known, deliberately-withheld example: its warmDigestCache() step defaults to fetching https://api.worldmonitor.app when API_BASE_URL is unset, so auto-enabling it here would silently start making requests to a non-local host by default -- same category of risk as the excluded entry below. Add it only after setting API_BASE_URL to point at this sidecar, or after adding a local-mode-aware default to that script itself.",
